<title>LEBANON: Lebanon February money supply statistics.</title>
<headline>Lebanon February money supply statistics.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Lebanon released on Tuesday the latest statistics on money supply during the month of February (blns of Lebanese pounds at end of period):</p>
<p>				  M1	   M2	 M3	M4</p>
<p>1997</p>
<p>    Jan			1775	14328     29332   34313</p>
<p>    Feb			1803	14658     29692   34996</p>
<p>1996</p>
<p>    Jan			1516	10092     23162   26549</p>
<p>    Feb			1585	10366     23756   27201</p>
<p>The Bank defined the aggregates as follows:</p>
<p>M1 -- Currency in circulation + Demand deposits</p>
<p>M2 -- M1 + Other deposits in Lebanese pounds</p>
<p>M3 -- M2 + Deposits in F.X.</p>
<p>M4 -- M3 + Treasury bills held by the non-banking system</p>
<p>($1 = 1,547.75 Lebanese pounds in February)</p>
</text>
